[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886555998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120971#issuecomment-4886555998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120971","id":4886555998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0LtXg","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T15:26:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T08:41:14Z","body":"`OPCODE_CALL` has a parameter for the return value address but it is ignored in the VM. This is likely because it shares a setup with `OPCODE_CALL_RETURN`.\r\n\r\nI propose two alternative more-involved ways to implement this:\r\n\r\n1. Remove the return address line entirely for `OPCODE_CALL`.\r\n2. Combine `OPCODE_CALL_RETURN` and `OPCODE_CALL` into just one opcode. A `NIL` or `0` address signals the no-return version and is handled in the VM.\r\n\r\nThis pattern of using `CallTarget` to create temporaries for opcodes that may or may not use them is pretty common - though the vm behaviour varies - some assign a value, some ignore. I think we could unify the behaviour across opcodes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886555998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5010822147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120971#issuecomment-5010822147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120971","id":5010822147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKqsUAw","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T09:53:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T09:53:51Z","body":"Thoughts on if we can tackle the other opcodes? Some of the others have a return version (such as method bind) but their implementations and interfaces vary.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5010822147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_